print("""
================================================================================
                              CONCLUSIONS
================================================================================

1. PHASE LAG INVARIANCE
   The dimensionless curvature-migration phase lag (Δs/W ≈ 2.0) is statistically
   indistinguishable between regulated and unregulated rivers (p = 0.412).
   → The spatial template of erosion is a geometric property conserved under
     flow regulation.

2. MIGRATION RATE SUPPRESSION
   Median migration rates are 54% lower in the regulated river (0.67 vs 1.45 m/yr,
   p < 0.001), with reduced variability (MAD: 1.48 vs 2.99, p = 0.002).
   → Regulation acts as a throttle on migration magnitude.

3. VEGETATION × REGULATION INTERACTION
   The LME model reveals a significant interaction (β = -0.33, p < 0.001):
   - Unregulated: ΔEVI effect weak (β = -0.08, p = 0.15)
   - Regulated: ΔEVI effect strong (β = -0.41, p < 0.001)
   → Vegetation becomes a primary constraint on bank retreat when flood peaks
     are suppressed.

4. GEOMORPHIC DORMANCY
   Bend-scale heterogeneity explains 38% of variance in log(E) (ICC = 0.38).
   → Rivers retain geometric capacity for migration but exhibit minimal realized
     movement under regulation.

5. MANAGEMENT IMPLICATIONS
   Effective restoration requires both reinstatement of hydraulic driving forces
   and active management of reinforced bank resistance.

================================================================================
LIMITATIONS
================================================================================
- Single dam-pair comparison within a Coastal Plain setting
- Findings require testing across diverse dam types and climatic regimes
- Sediment starvation effects not fully resolved
- Three temporal snapshots may miss short-term variability

================================================================================
DATA AVAILABILITY
================================================================================
All code and data are available at:
https://github.com/thapawan/invariant-meander-dam-regulation
""")

